OL,3,AIndia's costliest film retells a
OL,4,Abeloved Hindu epic - but divides
OL,5,Acritics
OL,6,
OL,7,FIndia's most expensive film - a lavish
OL,8,Fretelling of the Hindu epic Ramayana,
OL,9,Fmade in two parts for a reported $500m
OL,10,F(#370m) - has opened in cinemas
OL,11,Fworldwide, sparking enormous
OL,12,Fexpectations and mixed reviews.
OL,14,FDirected by Nitesh Tiwari, Ramayana:
OL,15,FRise of a Legend is the first of two
OL,16,Fplanned films, a sprawling production
OL,17,Fthat brings together some of India's
OL,18,Fbiggest stars, Hollywood visual-effects
OL,19,Fexpertise and two Oscar-winning
OL,20,Fcomposers in an attempt to take one of
OL,21,Fthe country's most revered stories to a
OL,22,Fglobal audience.
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,180,160,200,105,0,100
